export declare const EJECTED_CONTENT = "# Ejected from Flisk\n\n`flisk eject` wrote this file and nothing else. It did not copy, move or generate anything, and it did\nnot remove Flisk. What exists is what Flisk had already generated, and that is still Flisk-owned output.\n\n## Where the generated files are\n\n- `.flisk/.flisk-out/` holds the Tiltfile and the engine it loads (`flisk-cli-ext/`). It is git-ignored.\n  `flisk config regenerate` rewrites the master files in it.\n- The golden-layer Dockerfile and the Traefik file (`.flisk/.flisk-out/`) are\n  written by Tilt when it runs, not by `flisk eject`. Until Tilt has run they do not exist. They are git-ignored.\n- The per-service files in `services/<stack>/<name>/.autogenerated/` (Compose, Dockerfile, and the\n  `.flisk-contract/` snapshots that `flisk config verify` compares them with) are also written when\n  Tilt runs. Whether Git tracks them depends on your `.gitignore`: `flisk project` adds\n  `services/**/.autogenerated/` to it, while older projects may not have that line. Where they are\n  ignored, a fresh checkout or CI has no snapshots, so `flisk config verify` reports them missing until\n  `flisk up` has regenerated the files.\n- Your own Dockerfiles, `service.json` files and source code are untouched.\n\n## Running the stack without the flisk CLI\n\nThere is no Tiltfile at the project root, so a plain `tilt up` does not find one. Flisk runs:\n\n    tilt up -f .flisk/.flisk-out/Tiltfile -- --focus=<stack>\n\nfrom the project root (`<stack>` is a stack name under `services/`; without `--focus` the Tiltfile\nfalls back to its default phase). The Tiltfile still reads `.flisk/project.json` and the\n`service.json` files, so those must stay. `flisk up` also does steps before Tilt starts (it chooses\nhost ports and exports them to Tilt); running Tilt by hand skips them.\n\n## Cleaning up\n\nOptional to delete later: this file, and `.flisk/` plus the `service.json` files if you stop using Flisk.\nDeleting them also removes what the Tiltfile needs.\n\nTo go back to Flisk: install the version named by `pinnedFliskVersion` in `.flisk/project.json` (if set), then run `flisk config regenerate`.\n";
